task: conversation-over-frame
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-04
branch: feature/conversation-over-frame
worktree: ../okay-wt-conv

why: Two slot models appeared in this repository in one day, and the
  consumer of the older one asked for the merge rather than a rival.
  Each has exactly what the other lacks: okay.intent has the FRAME
  (typed values, answer-by-name, missing), okay.agent.Conversation has
  the SUSPENSION (a straight-line intake parked in a journal across a
  restart). Conversation should hang over okay.intent.Frame and drop
  its own Slot/Frame.

fixes, all named by the consumer as an open request or a live defect:
  1. their Slot.read returns Option[Json] and the text is re-parsed
     later — the same defect intent-frame-typed-values just closed
  2. Conversation.answer only answers the pending question, so
     "Wroclaw, and remote works" fills the city and re-asks the terms;
     Frame.answer takes a slot by NAME and the primitive is there
  3. Say.Ask cannot say how many questions remain; Frame.missing can

operator warning from the consumer, to be honoured: the LANGUAGE must
  be an argument of the whole conversation, not a parameter of every
  call. Slot.question(lang) and Frame.answer(name, lang, text) make a
  mid-intake language flip possible by accident — they measured one,
  on the second-to-last question. The frame must CARRY the language.

open question to settle first: okay-intent's test scope depends on
  okay-agent (Rerun/FileVersions replay), so okay-agent depending on
  okay-intent may be a project cycle. Verify with sbt before designing
  around it.

files: okay-intent/src/main/scala/okay/intent/Slot.scala,
  okay-agent/src/main/scala/okay/agent/Conversation.scala, build.sbt,
  both test trees, okay-demo, specs/{intent-classify,conversation}.md
